{"y":1983,"label":"1982–83","coach":"Dom Perno","conf":"Big East","confShort":"Big East","w":12,"l":16,"cw":5,"cl":11,"confFinish":"7th in Big East","finish":"none","srs":2.81,"sos":3.81,"ortg":94.3,"drtg":95.7,"ppg":70.5,"oppg":71.5,"story":{"headline":"Earl Kelley, Big East Rookie of the Year","text":"With Corny Thompson, Mike McKay and Chuck Aleksinas graduated and drafted, Perno's sixth team leaned on youth, and freshman guard Earl Kelley of New Haven delivered 16.7 points per game and UConn's first Big East Rookie of the Year award. Junior Karl Hobbs (11.8 points) and senior Bruce Kuczenski (9.8 points, 6.8 rebounds) supplied experience. UConn opened 7–2, splitting two games at the Fiesta Classic in Tempe, beating Air Force and Texas A&M to win its own Connecticut Mutual Classic, and winning 71–67 at Pittsburgh in the Panthers' first Big East season. But the new 16-game league schedule was brutal: the Huskies lost 13 of 15 games between January 6 and February 21, 11 of them to Big East opponents and seven to ranked teams. They finished with a flourish, winning at Providence and at Seton Hall and upsetting No. 18 Syracuse 55–54 in Hartford, then lost 69–68 to No. 13 Villanova in the Big East quarterfinals at Madison Square Garden. The 12–16 record was UConn's first losing season since Perno's first year.","moments":[{"date":"1982-12-29","title":"Connecticut Mutual Classic champions","text":"UConn beats Texas A&M 69–63 to win its holiday tournament at the Hartford Civic Center."},{"date":"1983-03-05","title":"Upset of Syracuse","text":"UConn closes the regular season by beating No. 18 Syracuse 55–54 at the Hartford Civic Center."},{"date":"1983-03-10","title":"One-point Big East exit","text":"No. 13 Villanova edges UConn 69–68 in the Big East quarterfinals at Madison Square Garden."}],"honors":["Earl Kelley – Big East Rookie of the Year","Earl Kelley – Big East All-Freshman team"],"sources":["https://uconnhuskies.com/documents/download/2026/8/13/RECORD_BOOK_26-27_V2_.pdf","https://www.sports-reference.com/cbb/schools/connecticut/men/1983-schedule.html","https://12thman.com/sports/mens-basketball/schedule/season/1982-83","https://archive.org/details/1982-University-of-Connecticut-Mutual-Classic-Basketball-Program-Lafayette-AM","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_East_Conference_(1979%E2%80%932013)"]},"roster":[{"pid":"earl-kelley-1","name":"Earl Kelley","num":"10","cls":"FR","pos":"G","ht":"6-1","wt":177,"home":"New Haven, CT","pg":{"g":27,"gs":16,"mp":31.6,"pts":16.7,"trb":2.3,"ast":2.4,"stl":1.5,"blk":0.0,"tov":2.0,"fg_pct":0.446,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.743,"orb":null,"pf":1.7},"tot":{"mp":853,"fg":169,"fga":379,"fg3":null,"fg3a":null,"ft":113,"fta":152,"orb":null,"drb":null,"trb":61,"ast":64,"stl":41,"blk":0,"tov":55,"pf":46,"pts":451,"g":27},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.5,"efg_pct":null,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":null,"ws_per_40":null,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null},"verified":["record_book"]},{"pid":"karl-hobbs-2","name":"Karl Hobbs","num":"14","cls":"JR","pos":"G","ht":"5-8","wt":160,"home":"Cambridge, MA","photo":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d1/Karl_Hobbs_in_2007.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","photoWide":true,"pg":{"g":28,"gs":27,"mp":30.8,"pts":11.8,"trb":1.6,"ast":4.1,"stl":1.7,"blk":0.1,"tov":3.4,"fg_pct":0.532,"fg3_pct":null,"ft_pct":0.828,"orb":null,"pf":3.3},"tot":{"mp":863,"fg":124,"fga":233,"fg3":null,"fg3a":null,"ft":82,"fta":99,"orb":null,"drb":null,"trb":46,"ast":114,"stl":47,"blk":2,"tov":95,"pf":93,"pts":330,"g":28},"adv":{"per":null,"ts_pct":0.589,"efg_pct":null,"usg_pct":null,"ast_pct":null,"trb_pct":null,"stl_pct":null,"blk_pct":null,"ws":null,"ws_per_40":null,"bpm":null,"obpm":null,"dbpm":null},"verified":["record_book"]},{"pid":"bruce-kuczenski-1","name":"Bruce Kuczenski","num":"23","cls":"SR","pos":"F","ht":"6-10","wt":230,"home":"Bristol, CT","pg":{"g":28,"gs"